# Model Diagram Validation

When generating or modifying model diagrams, validate every node and edge:

## Input Nodes
- Every synthetic input node must connect to ALL consumers (children that receive external input)
- If a module has >1 input port, create labeled synthetic input nodes using the port names from the module's forward() signature
- Input nodes must have shape annotations when the module contains subgraphs

## Output Nodes
- Every synthetic output node must connect from exactly one operation or synthetic node
- If a module has >1 output, create labeled synthetic output nodes
- Output nodes must have shape annotations when the module contains subgraphs

## Expanded Modules
- Custom (non-torch.nn) leaf modules must be FX-expanded into their actual tensor operations
- Weight access (get_attr) and dtype access (getattr) nodes must be hidden
- Child modules not referenced by a parent's FX graph (inlined by FX) must be skipped
- FX-expanded modules must have synthetic @input and @output nodes inside their namespace

## Edge Validation
- Every edge must correspond to actual dataflow in the source code or model graph
- No cross-boundary edges between unrelated modules (e.g. vision ↔ language model loops)
- No broken edges (source node ID must exist in the graph)
- FX-derived edges override call-graph/sequential wiring for composite children
- When a composite's output rewiring runs, only rewire edges that still point to the original source

## Structural Rules
- ModuleList/Sequential containers do not get synthetic I/O nodes
- Top-level wrapper modules (language_model, visual) DO get I/O nodes
- I/O nodes use the namespace where children actually live, not a deeper sub-namespace
- Parallel layer groups (e.g. 3 types of decoder blocks) display as parallel branches, not sequential
